 =?UTF-8?q?ritical-length=20chain=20insertion=20on=20placed=20nets?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The buffering engine decomposes fanout, never distance: a single-sink
net spanning 500um gets at most one buffer at the sink, so
wire-dominated nets stay outside NLDM characterization regardless of
drive (slew violations on a large unrepaired design were
unmoved by max-drive sizing). repeater [-L um] splits every located
driver->sink edge longer than Lcrit with ceil(d/L)-1 chained buffers
at interpolated coordinates; the buffer variant is chosen so
max_out_cap covers one segment. Smoke: on a long single-sink net
the placed-view delay and the worst cap drop severalfold, CEC
equivalent. v1 limits: per-edge chains (no trunk sharing), unlocated
PIs skipped, 16-stage cap.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
